<%= UiComponents::Lookbook::TableOfContents.call(page) %>

Shows where the current page sits in a hierarchy - a trail of links ending in the current page.
[Appica docs](https://appica.dev/ui/components/react/breadcrumb)

<%= embed UI::BreadcrumbPreview, :default %>

## Usage

```ruby
Breadcrumb do
  BreadcrumbList do
    BreadcrumbItem { BreadcrumbLink(href: root_path) { "Home" } }
    BreadcrumbSeparator()
    BreadcrumbItem { BreadcrumbLink(href: projects_path) { "Projects" } }
    BreadcrumbSeparator()
    BreadcrumbItem { BreadcrumbLink(active: true) { @project.name } }
  end
end
```

Plain semantic parts with no state - lay the trail out yourself:

- `Breadcrumb` - the `<nav>` landmark (named "Breadcrumb", translated; `aria_label:` overrides).
- `BreadcrumbList` - the `<ol>`, wrapping on narrow screens.
- `BreadcrumbItem` - one `<li>`.
- `BreadcrumbLink` - an `<a>`; `active: true` makes it the current page (a `<span>` with `aria-current="page"`).
- `BreadcrumbSeparator` - a chevron (flipped under RTL) unless given content.
- `BreadcrumbEllipsis` - "…" for collapsed crumbs.

For switching between sibling views use Tabs or Navigation instead.

